title: Proposition 45
---
order: 45
---
short_label: X.45
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: A major straight line is divided at one point only.
----
proof:

Let *AB* be a major straight line divided at *C*, so that *AC* and *CB* are incommensurable in square, and let the sum of the squares on *AC* and *CB* be rational, but the rectangle *AC* by *CB* medial.

I say that *AB* is not so divided at another point.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="250" height="70" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.45 diagram" src="propX45.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "X.45",
        elements: [
            "A0;point;free;-1000,40;0;0",
            "A3;point;free;1000,40;0;0",
            "A;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,30,0",
            "B;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,220,0",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B;0;0",
            "C;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,170,0",
            "D;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,130,0"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

If possible, let it also be divided at *D*, so that *AD* and *DB* are incommensurable in square and the sum of the squares on *AD* and *DB* is rational, but the rectangle contained by them medial.

Then, since that by which the sum of the squares on *AC* and *CB* differs from the sum of the squares on *AD* and *DB* is also that by which twice the rectangle *AD* by *DB* differs from twice the rectangle *AC* by *CB*, while the sum of the squares on *AC* and *CB* exceeds the sum of the squares on *AD* and *DB* by a rational area, for both are rational, therefore twice the rectangle *AD* by *DB* also exceeds twice the rectangle *AC* by *CB* by a rational area, though they are medial, which is impossible. [!just X.26]

Therefore a major straight line is not divided at different points. Therefore it is only divided at one and the same point.

Therefore, *a major straight line is divided at one point only.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
----
guide: This proposition is not used in the rest of the *Elements*.
